Pietersz","alias":"Managing Director GCB","info":["Employee ID: EMP-ID RVB","pietersz_c@cga.cw","GCB account created Mar 22, 2024"]},{"stage":"Conditionally Issued","date":"2025-11-06","reviewer":"Sulmahine Penza-Kwidama","alias":"CGA USER 59","info":["Employee ID: CGA USER 59","Penza_s@cga.cw","GCB account created Nov 5, 2025"]}],"checklists":[{"name":"Application Verification Review","criticality":"Critical","items":[{"title":"Enigma Holding B.V. (Holding Company)","tag":"Share Ledger","criticality":"Critical","due":"2024-07-03","description":"Document is missing","notes":null},{"title":"Enigma Holding B.V. (Holding Company)","tag":"Director's List","criticality":"Critical","due":"2024-07-03","description":"Document is missing","notes":null},{"title":"Corvin Nagtegaal","tag":"Miscellaneous","criticality":"Critical","due":"2024-07-03","description":"PHDF is missing","notes":null},{"title":"Corvin Nagtegaal","tag":"Miscellaneous","criticality":"Critical","due":"2024-07-03","description":"Enclosures are missing","notes":null},{"title":"Enigma Holding B.V. (Holding Company)","tag":"Share Ledger","criticality":"Critical","due":"2024-09-20","description":"Share Ledger and Director list are missing, kindly submit the requested documents.","notes":null},{"title":"Enigma Holding B.V. (Holding Company)","tag":"Director's List","criticality":"Critical","due":"2024-07-03","description":"Director list is missing, kindly submit the requested document","notes":null},{"title":"PAGE 6: QUESTION 34 - Online Gaming Application Form","tag":"Question","criticality":"Minor","due":"2024-10-29","description":"The company name was filled in on the Online Gaming application form instead of the name of the portal administrator as the contact person. Kindly update the form with the appointed contact person and resubmit it.","notes":null},{"title":"PAGE 6: QUESTION 36 - Online Gaming Application Form","tag":"Question","criticality":"Minor","due":"2024-10-29","description":"The passport number of the contact person is missing. Kindly fill the passport number in Question 36 and resubmit the form.","notes":null},{"title":"PAGE 6: QUESTION 38 - Online Gaming Application Form","tag":"Question","criticality":"Minor","due":"2024-10-29","description":"The Online gaming application form has an incomplete contact address in Question 38. Kindly complete Question 38 and resubmit the form.","notes":null},{"title":"PAGE 7: DECLARATION AND DATA PRIVACY - Online Gaming Application Form","tag":"Question","criticality":"Minor","due":"2024-10-29","description":"The Online gaming application form must have the Declaration and data privacy on page 7 named by the contact person. Kindly fill the Declaration and resubmit the Form.","notes":null},{"title":"Nixxe B.V. - Financial Statement","tag":"Financial Audit","criticality":"Critical","due":"2024-10-31","description":"We are missing Financial Statement of Nixxe B.V. Kindly submit the requested document.","notes":null}]},{"name":"Application Due Diligence Review","criticality":"Critical","items":[{"title":"QPA/2024/01221 - Lorenza Godett - PHDF","tag":"Miscellaneous","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-02-05","description":"The PHDF must be signed and verified digitally. Please resubmit.","notes":null},{"title":"QPA/2024/00894 - Christopher van Rosberg - PHDF","tag":"Miscellaneous","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-02-05","description":"The PHDF must be signed and verified digitally. Please resubmit.","notes":null},{"title":"Compliance Officer","tag":"Miscellaneous","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-02-12","description":"No CO appointed. Appoint a CO fluent in AML and submit their PHDF as a key person together with a CV and letter of engagement. No SOW required.","notes":null},{"title":"Financial Statements","tag":"Financial Audit","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-02-12","description":"Submit FS for years ending 2022 and 2023, as well as accounts for year 2024 which are not older than 6 months.","notes":null},{"title":"Corporate Structure","tag":"Miscellaneous","criticality":"Medium","due":"2025-02-12","description":"Corporate structure is unsigned. Resubmit signed by director.","notes":null},{"title":"Source of Funds of Business","tag":"Source of Funds","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-02-12","description":"Submit enhanced documentation as to how the operations of the business are funded and by whom, including documents which evidence funds owned by the company through cash flow or other means, such as wallets. All documents submitted must be duly certified.","notes":null},{"title":"Player Registration","tag":"Player Registration","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-02-13","description":"One of the registered domains vulkanspiele.com's registration form does not require the player's name, address, country or DOB. This information must be collected at the latest prior to the first deposit. Kindly amend.","notes":null},{"title":"Prohibited Jurisdictions","tag":"Prohibiited Countries","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-02-13","description":"It was noted that a player is able to register an account on 64betcasino.com and spinrolla.com by selecting Curacao and Netherlands as their country of residence, even though these countries are listed in the prohibited jurisdictions list in the T&Cs. Kindly amend.","notes":null},{"title":"AML Policy","tag":"Miscellaneous","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-02-13","description":"The AML policy must adhere to Curacao AML laws. Kindly amend.","notes":null},{"title":"Registered domains","tag":"Operations","criticality":"Critical","due":"2025-02-13","description":"The footer indicates that the registered domains are operated by Kaurum Limited, a Cyprus registered entity. Please note that the registered domains must be operated by the Curacao registered applicant company. Kindly clarify and amend.","notes":null},{"title":"QPA/2026/04555 - Mihaita Cotea - SOW","tag":"Source of Wealth","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-03-05","description":"Please upload an enhanced SOW to your base application to support all applications.","notes":null}]},{"name":"AML Policy","criticality":"Critical","items":[{"title":"Signature of CO and Managing director","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"High","due":"2026-05-29","description":"The policy must be signed by the Compliance officer and Managing director of the applicant.","notes":null},{"title":"Business Risk Assessment (BRA)","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-05-29","description":"The operator must conduct a comprehensive risk assessment of business operations which is to be included in the AML Policy. This should outline the assessment carried out to identify the ML/TF risks the operator is exposed to and ensure that the policies, controls and procedures adopted are adequate to prevent and mitigate those risks. The risk assessment should address the ways in which the casino’s products and services, type of customers, delivery channels and geographical factors could be used to launder money, finance terrorism and finance proliferation, and the extent of the risk that this will happen. In this respect the casino should indicate risk it is prepared to accept. Furthermore, it should indicate how effectiveness of the measures to mitigate risks are monitored and improved. Revision of the BRA should happen whenever changes occur to the operating environment, otherwise once a year. The BRA should be documented and approved by management. Technological development risk assessment should be carried out prior to launch of new products, business practices, delivery mechanism or new technologies.","notes":null},{"title":"Customer Due Diligence (CDD) (XCG 4000 threshold)","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-05-29","description":"The policy must describe timing and which measures are used for customer due diligence including PEP and sanction screening. Further describe the actions taken when XCG 4,000 is reached, but not all documents have been submitted by the player. Describe what happens if the requested information is still not received within 30 days of reaching the threshold. Describe the process if the business relationship needs to be terminated. Describe the timing of ongoing sanctions screening (UN and EU list) and the procedure followed for freezing of funds and reporting to competent authorities in Curacao. Describe how threshold is calculated.","notes":null},{"title":"Crypto Policy","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-05-29","description":"The policy must define the rules and risk controls around virtual assets and crypto usage.","notes":null},{"title":"Reporting to FIU Curacao (XCG 5000)","tag":"Policy Document","criticality":"Critical","due":"2026-05-29","description":"The policy must describe the process in place to recognise and report unusual transactions to the Curacao FIU when the threshold of XCG 5,000 is reached. It is important to note the prohibition to disclose a report filed to the FIU. The record keeping requirements for CDD information and transactions also need to be described.","notes":null}]}]}]}